  "decisions": {
    "k-fees": {
      "decision": "created",
      "reason": "Created n-creator-fee-routing. MarsX (\"Fees to @arikuschnir via UsePaid\", $4.87M), TeleMoney/TM (\"fees redirected to any telegram username\", $657K), Pepper The Raccoon (\"redirecting fees to his Owner\", $586K), slopcannon (\"Fees to @boneGPT via UsePaid\", $370K), Cashed Money (\"Fees to @GetCashedMoney via Cashed\", $143K) and WIRED (\"fees wired to social media accounts\", $112K) are six coins on three covered launchpads (pump.fun, pons, Flap) whose metadata names the routing, about $6.7M in 24h token volume at discovery. Sources beyond metadata: usepaid.app (e3:0) describes the mechanism; @TeleMoneySOL posts 2026-10-10 to 2026-10-12 (e3:3) report 108 coins and 17,411 GRAM paid out; @PickACycle 2026-10-12 and @Joindotfun 2026-10-07 (e3:1) show other tools using the same idea. These are the projects' own sources, the same bar the credits narrative met on 2026-10-12; flagged for the owner. SOLVE (fees reward agents), BOTS, VSWAP and HARMONIC share the word but not the mechanism. It replaces Post-quantum at the cap.",
      "narrativeId": "n-creator-fee-routing"
    },
    "k-creator": {
      "decision": "assigned",
      "reason": "The word creator over [ss] (an AI TV station coin, no fee story), HARMONIC (an agent that claims its own creator fees and burns them, not a routing tool) and CASHED, which belongs to n-creator-fee-routing through k-fees; [ss] and HARMONIC are not added.",
      "narrativeId": "n-creator-fee-routing"
    },
    "k-agents": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "HIRE ($8.2M, created 2026-10-12; metadata only \"Launched on discord.gg/uxento\") is described in posts as a launchpad where coins pair with HIRE and AI agents market them (e2:0), but its metadata names no story and the posts are promotion and caller posts; SOLVE (governance token; fees reward agents), ZEREBRO (a 2022-era agent memecoin) and WISP (agentic finance infrastructure) are unrelated products. Revisit HIRE if its metadata or an independent source names a pairing mechanism that other coins share."
    },
    "k-fund": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "The word fund/reserve over HUMPH (a camel meme: \"Humphrey was born with one [a reserve]\"; the posts are caller posts, e2:2), AODF (the oil/dividend-fund lead, still deferred) and BOTS (a bot launchpad). No shared story; AODF volume fell from $16.6M to $1.8M and the other oil/dividend-fund pools remain flagged by the new-pool rules."
    },
    "k-stocks": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "STONK (StonkFun's token, \"Backed by stocks\", $3.6M) and OTC (\"earn stocks, pre-ipo, and yield\", $412K) stay deferred: the posts found for STONK are launchpad promotion from August and September (e2:3), and neither describes a tokenized-stock product like the Robinhood Stock Token apps; RAETO (\"Your tokenized stocks pay for your AI inference\") has a $68K market cap, under the $100K member bar. VERDEX (a tokenized-markets marketplace the word match missed) was added to n-tokenized-assets."
    },
    "k-platform": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "Generic word over REA (reverse-engineering tool, a caller-pumped coin), MOBY (a token-discovery app token), BOTS (bot launchpad), VSWAP (private swaps) and ZEREBRO. No shared story; the platform posts found are caller posts (e2:4)."
    },
    "k-anything": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "Generic word over REA (\"Reverse engineer anything\", two pools), CHILLGUY and 灭霸. No shared story."
    },
    "k-market": {
      "decision": "rejected",
      "reason": "Generic word over Bear (\"The market just shifted to extreme fear\"), ANUBIS (market intelligence) and POLAR (an AI insight ecosystem on Robinhood Chain). No shared story; the posts are caller posts (e2:5)."
    },
    "k-used": {
